// Used only by `build:types`, never by `typecheck`.
//
// tsup builds declarations through rollup-plugin-dts, and hardcodes
// `baseUrl: compilerOptions.baseUrl || "."` into the options it hands that
// plugin (tsup 8.5.1, dist/rollup.js). TypeScript 6 deprecated `baseUrl` and
// reports setting it as error TS5101, so the declaration build fails on an
// option this package never asked for and cannot unset. tsup has no newer
// release that drops it.
//
// Scoping the acknowledgement to this file keeps `tsc --noEmit` strict about
// deprecated options in our own configuration: if we ever set a deprecated
// option ourselves, the typecheck still fails on it.
//
// This expires with TypeScript 7, which removes `baseUrl` outright and will
// reject "6.0" as a value here. At that point tsup must be fixed or replaced.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "ignoreDeprecations": "6.0"
  }
}
